# Go
/vantage
*.test
*.out

# web/dist — the built frontend — is NOT tracked. It was until 2026-09-01, so
# that `go install …@latest` (which builds from whatever git holds, with no npm)
# got a real frontend rather than the "Frontend bundle not found." placeholder
# //go:embed happily produces from an empty directory.
#
# The cost of tracking a derived artifact is that it can disagree with its
# sources, and only a CI assertion noticed — after the drift was committed, and
# with no way for dependabot to fix a bundle its bumps had changed. Nothing
# derived is tracked now, so nothing can drift.
#
# `go install` still works at a tag, because `just release` builds the bundle
# into a commit that exists only on the tag. On main there is no bundle: run
# `just web-sync` (or `just build`) to make one locally. It stays ignored.
# See docs/design/pypi-distribution.md §4.1.
web/dist/*
!web/dist/.gitkeep

